Sure! Here's an example of how to create a VPC for infrastructure as code with two subnets using the Terraform language:

First, we will create a VPC:
```java
resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "192.168.0.0/16"
}
```
Next, we will create two subnets within the VPC:
```java
resource "aws_subnet" "private" {
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block = "192.168.1.0/24"
}

resource "aws_subnet" "public" {
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block = "192.168.2.0/24"
}
```
And that's it! You now have a VPC with two subnets, one private and one public. You can use this code to create the VPC and subnets in your AWS account using Terraform.
